  "body": "Vendors `francoisgn/agentic-harness` 0.1.0 (the framework distilled from this repo's `docs/agents/*`, lots and labels, plus Crédit Immo's issue workflow) so the maintainer's projects share one versioned set of rules.\n\n## What changes\n- `.harness/`: framework docs (French; `ESSENTIEL.md` in English), label taxonomy, hooks, `VERSION`, `lock` (commit + SHA-256 per file), `config.json` (language `en`, integration branch `dev-swift`, exclusions).\n- `.claude/skills/`: `lot-start`, `lot-finish`, `review-round`, `lessons-check`, `harness-update`.\n- `.claude/settings.json`: session-start reminder + `guard-git` (refuses force-push, push to `master`/`dev-swift`, `--no-verify`).\n- Managed `<!-- harness:begin cadre -->` blocks at the end of `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md`; project rules win.\n- Not vendored (this repo already has better): issue forms, PR template, lot template, markdownlint config, labels; framework workflows are skipped because `ezzz` cannot call a private repo's reusable workflows.\n\n`harness-sync.sh --check` → 🟢 up to date.\n\n## Watch points\n- 🟠 `guard-git` blocks direct pushes to `dev-swift` from agent sessions — intended, but any automation that pushed there from Claude sessions must go through PRs.\n- 🟠 Framework docs besides `ESSENTIEL.md` are in French.\n- Updates: `/harness-update` or `harness-sync.sh --ref vX.Y.Z --target .`, as a draft PR.\n\nRefs #562\nClaim: cloud/stoic-edison-cj20yp\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHqnZEd6mhkmo2RqSU)_",
